# Allowlist for scripts/check_method_registry.sh.
#
# Format:
#   <method-id> <ticket-id>     # rationale
#
# Comments: everything after `#` is ignored.
#
# Each entry MUST cite the ticket that wires the method via
# `populate_method_registry` (src/plugins/simulation.rs) and matches
# its frontmatter `wires-method:` to the method id. When the work
# lands, drop the entry; the lint will then re-enforce the
# bidirectional check. Adding a new entry without a ticket id is a
# code-review failure.
#
# Empty at landing of ticket 319 — the registry is empty by design;
# the first PendingSubstrate method to land (in tickets 320+) is the
# first real exercise of the bidirectional check, and should land
# with its glue ticket's `wires-method:` frontmatter intact rather
# than via allowlist.
#
# Discipline reference: CLAUDE.md §"Bugfix discipline" /
# "Every dormant method has a glue ticket."
# Parallel precedent: scripts/influence_map_registry.allowlist (207),
# scripts/substrate_stubs.allowlist (160).
